# Drafted by Gemini (R11 batch b4), edited. thomasin_ardor's first conversation.

~ start
set thomasin_ardor_met
Narrator: Pins glint in a velvet cushion, and the room is hushed save for the crisp snip of shears. Thomasin measures your cloak with one cool, unblinking glance.
thomasin_ardor [neutral]: Welcome to A Stitch in Time. Wipe the moor-mud from your boots before you step upon the drop-cloth, if you please.
-> menu

~ menu
thomasin_ardor [neutral]: How may I be of service to you?
* Browse their wares -> shop_open
* Ask about the silk patterns pinned to the wall -> work
* Ask why the villagers rarely linger here -> village
* [Perception DC 14] Examine the pale scars and hare-pin at her collar -> secret_ok | secret_fail
* Take our leave -> END

~ shop_open
thomasin_ardor [smile]: Look closely at the seams on your travels, and bring me any strange cloth you find. I can mend homespun or cobble a split boot while you wait.
shop
-> menu

~ work
thomasin_ardor [sad]: Those are courtly cuts I drafted for velvet and silver thread. Folk here only ever order grey wool coats and mourning bands.
-> menu

~ village
thomasin_ardor [weary]: Small towns enjoy small tales, and I do not care to chatter at the well. They call me proud, which leaves me peace to sew.
-> menu

~ secret_ok
Narrator: Beneath her high lace collar runs a neat, surgical seam across her throat, pinned with a tiny pewter hare bearing antlers.
thomasin_ardor [neutral]: I fell through a greenhouse pane as a girl, and Master Randall stitched my life back together. He says his quiet friends have great need of my needle.
-> menu

~ secret_fail
thomasin_ardor [neutral]: It is only an old childhood scratch and a trinket from a kind neighbour. Nothing that concerns a passing customer.
-> menu
